# Summary
Introduced: startup validation was added in this commit and made the pre-existing bounded digest sentinel fatal on reopen, while the normal online update path still persists that sentinel after 128 commands.
The new LocalClusterMap startup path validates every PG replica before the storage cluster is returned. PgStore::validate_metadata_command_replay_state now treats METADATA_STATE_DIGEST_UNVERIFIED as a fatal error. However, online_metadata_state_digest intentionally returns that same sentinel once applied_log_index exceeds METADATA_STATE_DIGEST_ONLINE_COMMAND_LIMIT, which is 128. Therefore, normal metadata activity beyond 128 commands in any PG persists state_digest = 0, and the next process restart will fail during StorageCluster::open_local_nodes. This creates a latent persistent denial of service: an authenticated client able to perform metadata-mutating S3 operations, such as bucket/object/multipart state changes, can push a PG over the threshold and wait for or induce a restart/crash to prevent the server from coming back up.

