# Resolution
Fixed in `e77fe33` (`Fix restart validation for unverified metadata digest`).

Restart validation now treats `METADATA_STATE_DIGEST_UNVERIFIED` as an
intentional bounded-online-path marker rather than a fatal clean-open failure.
When a local PG has crossed the online digest limit, reopen walks the durable
command-log prefix, recomputes the full canonical materialized metadata digest,
persists that digest into `metadata_command_replica_state`, and only then
compares validated replica state across the acting set. Corrupt log entries,
hash-chain mismatches, materialized-row drift, missing replica state, and
replica disagreement still fail closed.

The regression
`local_cluster_reopen_recomputes_unverified_large_command_stream_digest` covers
a 129-command stream that stores the sentinel before shutdown and successfully
reopens only after recomputing and persisting matching full digests on all
replicas.

Verification for the fix:
- `cargo fmt`
- `cargo nextest run -p storage local_cluster_reopen_recomputes_unverified_large_command_stream_digest`
- `cargo nextest run -p storage`
- `./scripts/check-storage-cluster-boundaries`
- `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`
- `cargo nextest run`
